  "notes": [
    "Maximums and minimums are per every 1,000 points unless otherwise stated (p. 121). The builder applies them as written, which is right for armies up to 1,000 points; scale them up yourself for larger armies.",
    "Combined Grenadiers and Voltigeurs: the Grenadier (or Voltigeur) companies of a brigade's battalions can be massed. The parent battalions lose 1 Hand-to-Hand (or Mixed Formation); two battalions' companies make a Tiny unit, three or four a Small unit, six or more a standard one, for any infantry brigade. Not built here. The list's table makes them 7/3/4/3 (43 points) and 6/3/4/3 (45 points); the chapter (p. 56) makes them Small, 5/3/4/2.",
    "The Cavalry Brigade box also says up to half of a brigade's regiments must be Line Light cavalry, which its own same-class rule makes moot; the builder applies the same-class rule.",
    "An attached Horse battery costs 26 points in the brigade boxes, against 30 in the stat table. Half batteries cost half points, rounded up (Foot 14, Horse 13, Heavy 16), with the half battery stat line on p. 120 (2-1-1, Stamina 1).",
    "Named commanders have no official points cost in this supplement; they're priced here at the Divisional Commander cost for their Staff Rating, so adjust as you agree."
  ],
  "specialRules": [
    "A Marshal's baton in every knapsack: a commander who has it rolls for aggression, decisiveness and independence (Black Powder p. 94) on 1 Low, 2-4 Normal, 5-6 High.",
    "Pas de Charge: French infantry in Attack Column are Reliable, and a commander adds +1 to his Staff Rating ordering them in Attack Column (on top of the usual +1 for a column).",
    "French infantry: Must Form Square, Mixed Formation, Column of Companies (the British rule, p. 31), and can form skirmish order in terrain they couldn't normally enter.",
    "Cavalry Column of Attack: two bases wide, three deep. +1 Staff Rating to order it, −1 Hand-to-Hand, +1 combat resolution, artillery gets +1 to hit it, and it gains no Morale bonus. French cavalry can also fight in Line, Deep Formation and March Column.",
    "Grand Battery: batteries from the infantry brigades, cavalry brigades and Corps Artillery can join the Artillery Brigade (no more than six batteries). It deploys as a brigade and must, so far as possible, target the same enemy brigade."
